WEBVTT

00:34.027 --> 00:35.295
(This drama is a work of fiction.)

00:35.295 --> 00:36.530
(All characters, organizations,
and events in this drama are fictitious.)

00:36.530 --> 00:37.764
(This drama complied
with production guidelines...)

00:37.764 --> 00:38.999
(for filming child actors and animals.)

01:02.322 --> 01:04.624
How will I be able to help him?

01:16.603 --> 01:18.471
(The 7th Tongyeong
Open Water Swimming Competition)

01:18.471 --> 01:19.539
"Open water swimming?"

01:29.816 --> 01:36.456
(Episode 6
Azure Spring)

01:36.923 --> 01:39.693
(The 7th Tongyeong
Open Water Swimming Competition)

01:40.393 --> 01:41.494
Let's join this competition.

01:45.432 --> 01:46.666
That's so random.

01:48.401 --> 01:50.303
I only came because I wanted
to tell you that,

01:50.303 --> 01:51.838
and I did, so I'll get going now.

01:52.372 --> 01:54.207
Are you going to keep staying underwater?

01:56.209 --> 01:58.111
You're the one who told me
we have to let go...

02:00.447 --> 02:01.615
to come back up and survive.

02:13.226 --> 02:14.261
I'll teach you...

02:16.530 --> 02:17.564
how to float in water.

02:25.872 --> 02:26.840
Come on.

02:28.041 --> 02:29.209
Hurry.

02:34.047 --> 02:35.115
You remember the rules, right?

02:35.415 --> 02:37.150
You stay in the guest house,
I stay in the main house,

02:37.150 --> 02:39.152
we share the kitchen and bathroom,
and wash our own dishes.

02:39.152 --> 02:40.854
Why are you doing this to me?

02:42.489 --> 02:43.690
It's just...

02:43.690 --> 02:46.760
It's scary seeing a guy like you
looking so down.

02:50.197 --> 02:51.998
I want to make you smile.

03:01.007 --> 03:02.242
Gosh, I'm so hungry.

03:02.609 --> 03:04.845
Why don't we eat something first?

03:14.120 --> 03:17.090
To preserve food for a long time,
we need to freeze it.

03:50.624 --> 03:52.459
But if they're frozen for too long,

03:52.459 --> 03:53.960
it's hard to melt them.

04:47.347 --> 04:48.515
What are you waiting for?

04:48.515 --> 04:49.449
Come on.

05:15.175 --> 05:17.043
Now, high five!

05:18.311 --> 05:19.679
It's the same with our hearts.

05:20.514 --> 05:21.915
If they're frozen for too long,

05:22.883 --> 05:24.317
they don't melt easily.

05:43.170 --> 05:45.739
That's when we need a special remedy.

06:33.720 --> 06:34.654
Ta-da!

06:35.555 --> 06:37.257
Give it a taste.

06:41.962 --> 06:44.030
Thanks for the meal.

07:05.418 --> 07:06.586
Who cooked this?

07:07.153 --> 07:08.522
It's so delicious!

07:17.898 --> 07:19.366
Try this too.

07:34.347 --> 07:35.916
- Is it good?
- Yes.

07:37.551 --> 07:39.019
Eat up. Go on.

07:56.169 --> 07:57.304
That was a great meal.

08:09.216 --> 08:12.252
Have you always liked cats?

08:17.624 --> 08:18.925
I don't really like them.

08:20.794 --> 08:22.362
Ever since I came to this island,

08:22.996 --> 08:25.799
I kept noticing them,
so I've been feeding them. That's all.

08:28.869 --> 08:31.171
That's what we usually call...

08:31.905 --> 08:33.139
"liking," you know.

08:34.741 --> 08:35.775
Is that so?

08:36.109 --> 08:37.143
Of course.

08:38.178 --> 08:40.413
Who would feed someone
they don't even like?

08:40.413 --> 08:41.781
It's because they like them.

08:48.788 --> 08:49.723
That doesn't mean...

08:50.657 --> 08:52.792
I have a crush on you or anything.

08:57.164 --> 08:58.131
I know.

08:59.199 --> 09:00.767
There's no way you'd like a guy like me.

09:02.936 --> 09:04.237
What are you talking about?

09:05.005 --> 09:06.072
You're perfectly healthy,

09:06.673 --> 09:07.874
and you make a decent living.

09:08.875 --> 09:09.809
What more do you need?

09:13.380 --> 09:15.148
I'm an ex-con.

09:17.617 --> 09:19.219
I know.

09:26.993 --> 09:27.994
I ruined...

09:30.397 --> 09:32.332
two people's lives.

09:37.771 --> 09:38.705
I...

09:39.840 --> 09:40.841
know that too.

09:43.710 --> 09:45.645
Your stalker fan...

09:47.180 --> 09:48.515
came to my house in Seoul.

09:52.219 --> 09:53.186
He asked me...

09:54.487 --> 09:55.922
to save you.

09:57.924 --> 09:59.993
And said that you smile
when you're with me.

10:18.445 --> 10:20.046
He was a junior I was fond of.

10:23.750 --> 10:24.951
He was soft-hearted,

10:25.719 --> 10:27.687
so military life didn't really suit him.

10:33.527 --> 10:34.561
And like always,

10:36.530 --> 10:38.231
the weak became a target...

10:41.601 --> 10:42.869
and got bullied.

10:46.806 --> 10:48.875
I couldn't bear to see that.

10:52.712 --> 10:54.047
So a man died,

10:56.683 --> 10:57.751
and another...

11:00.754 --> 11:02.355
was left barely alive.

11:09.529 --> 11:10.997
Sometimes I wonder...

11:16.736 --> 11:17.771
if I hadn't...

11:20.173 --> 11:21.575
tried to stop it,

11:26.713 --> 11:28.114
maybe he would've
just gotten beaten up a bit,

11:31.852 --> 11:34.754
or maybe broken a bone at worst.

11:37.123 --> 11:39.893
Maybe it would've just ended like that.

11:48.335 --> 11:49.202
Then...

11:53.907 --> 11:55.775
maybe Nam Seok U would've lived,

12:02.249 --> 12:04.184
and Jae Hui would be fine right now.

12:18.298 --> 12:19.166
No.

12:23.236 --> 12:25.305
It wouldn't have just ended with that.

12:28.175 --> 12:30.110
It would've gotten worse,

12:33.513 --> 12:34.748
and in the end,

12:38.451 --> 12:39.853
the results would've been the same.

12:44.424 --> 12:46.193
You did the right thing.

12:49.429 --> 12:50.831
What happened after that...

12:54.568 --> 12:55.869
was just an accident.

13:06.112 --> 13:07.514
It wasn't...

13:10.584 --> 13:11.685
your fault.

13:55.395 --> 13:56.696
It seems his habit of meddling...

13:57.697 --> 13:58.899
has rubbed off on me.

14:09.176 --> 14:12.512
The person who moved here
should be handing out rice cakes.

14:12.512 --> 14:13.780
Why am I the one bringing this?

14:14.414 --> 14:16.583
Hey, Seo Anna.
Dad sent me to give you rice cakes.

14:23.123 --> 14:24.457
Baek Su Jeong?

14:24.891 --> 14:25.926
Seo Anna.

14:26.493 --> 14:27.494
You...

14:36.303 --> 14:39.206
Su Jeong, it's not what you think.
We were just...

14:40.340 --> 14:42.576
chatting after our meal,
and we were so tired...

14:42.576 --> 14:44.110
How could you...

14:58.658 --> 14:59.593
Hey!

15:08.401 --> 15:09.369
Look at this.

15:10.103 --> 15:12.906
See? We were just discussing
this competition.

15:14.641 --> 15:15.876
That's right. The swimming competition.

15:16.142 --> 15:18.211
She suggested competing in this.

15:19.079 --> 15:21.648
You came back to Parang-ri
at the same time...

15:22.315 --> 15:24.584
and discussed
a swimming competition all night?

15:25.952 --> 15:26.887
Why?

15:27.420 --> 15:29.956
Well, if I'm going to live here...

15:30.757 --> 15:32.526
I need to earn a living.

15:33.326 --> 15:35.762
So I wanted to win the reward.

15:36.196 --> 15:37.230
Well, I get your reason.

15:38.431 --> 15:40.734
But why would you join, Deok Hyun?

15:41.001 --> 15:41.935
I'm not...

15:43.970 --> 15:46.706
I'm going to join with Ms. Seo.

15:51.912 --> 15:53.046
Then I want to join too.

15:53.914 --> 15:56.283
I can't bear to see you two
training together again.

15:58.785 --> 16:00.520
Well, sure...

16:01.388 --> 16:02.455
That's fine with me.

16:04.090 --> 16:05.025
Then I'll join too.

16:06.860 --> 16:08.562
Why did that guy...

16:08.562 --> 16:10.463
come all the way back here?

16:10.997 --> 16:14.234
He paid all the hospital fees
for our precious friend.

16:15.068 --> 16:17.137
So I'm thinking of winning the reward
and paying half of it.

16:18.171 --> 16:19.206
You'll let me join, right?

16:19.206 --> 16:20.040
Sure.

16:20.874 --> 16:21.708
No!

16:24.477 --> 16:27.214
I was the Black Unit's Piranha.

16:27.614 --> 16:28.748
One thing I'm confident in...

16:29.382 --> 16:31.051
is my swimming.

16:37.858 --> 16:39.526
Your chances of winning just dropped.

16:47.467 --> 16:52.906
(The 7th Tongyeong
Open Water Swimming Competition)

16:55.842 --> 16:57.777
- Shall we go?
- It looks beautiful. Let's go.

16:57.777 --> 16:59.813
(Swimming Competition Application)

17:09.222 --> 17:10.357
(Name: Yun Deok Hyun)

17:22.469 --> 17:23.904
(Parang-ri Street 5-1, Haedam-myeon
Tongyeong)

17:33.713 --> 17:36.816
(Signature)

17:44.958 --> 17:45.859
But...

17:47.594 --> 17:51.264
why do you want to teach me swimming?

17:54.935 --> 17:56.803
Why swimming of all things?

18:02.976 --> 18:04.010
All right!

18:04.010 --> 18:06.012
Think of the tissue as water.

18:06.780 --> 18:07.647
Move faster!

18:07.647 --> 18:09.349
Don't drop the tissue.

18:09.349 --> 18:10.750
I wanted to gift him...

18:11.985 --> 18:13.787
the moment of learning something.

18:14.888 --> 18:16.056
One, two!

18:16.923 --> 18:18.191
One, two!

18:18.758 --> 18:19.726
One, two!

18:20.627 --> 18:21.561
One, two!

18:22.395 --> 18:23.396
One, two!

18:23.396 --> 18:25.198
Keep your shoulders up!

18:27.200 --> 18:28.068
One, two!

18:29.970 --> 18:31.872
When I was learning diving from him...

18:33.006 --> 18:33.940
You're doing great!

18:34.307 --> 18:35.509
I couldn't think...

18:36.676 --> 18:38.645
of anything else in the moment,

18:44.718 --> 18:47.787
so I wanted to let him feel
that peace as well.

18:56.863 --> 18:58.965
I'm so hungry.

18:59.432 --> 19:02.235
How about some warm soup?

19:02.235 --> 19:04.104
Your face will get puffy
if you have soup at this hour.

19:04.104 --> 19:06.640
Then what do you usually eat at night?

19:06.640 --> 19:07.807
Salad.

19:07.807 --> 19:09.309
Right.

19:10.577 --> 19:13.146
Deok Hyun. What do you want to eat?

19:13.380 --> 19:14.981
Anything's fine with me.

19:16.483 --> 19:17.651
You're boring.

19:18.852 --> 19:19.886
Okay!

19:20.820 --> 19:22.689
Warm soup, salad,

19:23.089 --> 19:23.957
and anything.

19:24.524 --> 19:25.892
We'll have something we all like.

19:59.826 --> 20:02.062
Jeez. Clam soup is salty.

20:02.062 --> 20:04.097
My face is going to get all puffy.

20:07.567 --> 20:08.635
Damn it.

21:05.458 --> 21:06.660
Hey.

21:07.160 --> 21:09.629
Vegetables won't fill my stomach at all.

21:12.265 --> 21:13.133
Move over.

21:14.234 --> 21:15.902
You're hopeless.

21:19.840 --> 21:20.907
You can cook?

21:21.541 --> 21:23.844
I was the Black Unit's Frying Pan.

21:25.846 --> 21:26.680
You're pretty good.

22:05.886 --> 22:06.786
Ta-da!

22:08.555 --> 22:09.422
Wow.

22:10.290 --> 22:11.258
What is this?

22:12.659 --> 22:13.593
Pig slop?

22:14.694 --> 22:15.662
"Pig slop?"

22:16.129 --> 22:17.197
It's vegetable bibimbap!

22:17.631 --> 22:18.498
Right.

22:18.498 --> 22:20.600
It's better than a salad.

22:24.437 --> 22:26.740
Did you just throw in
whatever was in the fridge?

22:27.874 --> 22:29.109
Just try it before judging.

22:36.049 --> 22:37.250
All right, let's mix it.

22:37.250 --> 22:38.318
Go!

22:38.318 --> 22:39.286
Go!

22:44.291 --> 22:45.225
Come on.

22:49.129 --> 22:51.031
If we learn together
and get mixed up together...

22:52.432 --> 22:53.567
maybe things...

22:55.135 --> 22:55.969
will soften a bit,

22:57.804 --> 22:58.738
whether it's food,

23:00.207 --> 23:02.742
people, or scars.

23:08.448 --> 23:10.317
It's delicious. Try it.

23:11.084 --> 23:11.985
Maybe...

23:12.686 --> 23:14.087
things will be okay.

23:15.155 --> 23:17.290
Open up.

23:28.168 --> 23:29.135
Go on and try it.

23:29.135 --> 23:30.036
It's so good.

24:02.802 --> 24:04.104
I guess it's okay for pig slop.

24:05.605 --> 24:06.673
Pig slop?

24:07.507 --> 24:09.109
You just enjoyed it,
and you call it pig slop?

24:25.458 --> 24:26.393
Seo Anna...

24:27.127 --> 24:29.963
How dare you meet a guy like that
after dumping me?

24:37.704 --> 24:38.605
Yun Deok Hyun.

24:39.105 --> 24:40.006
Yun Deok Hyun!

24:45.545 --> 24:46.479
Yun Deok Hyun!

24:47.814 --> 24:48.748
Come out here!

24:49.449 --> 24:50.650
Are you here, Yun Deok Hyun?

24:58.124 --> 24:58.959
Chief.

24:59.526 --> 25:00.861
What brings you here?

25:00.861 --> 25:02.229
Baek Su Jeong, you little brat!

25:02.729 --> 25:05.131
Why were you sleeping here
instead of at home?

25:06.399 --> 25:07.667
Dad!

25:07.667 --> 25:08.668
I'm not a kid, you know.

25:08.668 --> 25:10.971
What's so wrong with sleeping
at a friend's on this tiny island?

25:10.971 --> 25:12.739
It's not that...

25:13.306 --> 25:14.741
Yun Deok Hyun lives here!

25:15.642 --> 25:17.544
What about Yun Deok Hyun?

25:17.811 --> 25:19.579
He's been living here for a while.

25:19.579 --> 25:20.580
Well, he...

25:22.449 --> 25:23.316
Hey.

25:24.417 --> 25:25.318
There he is.

25:25.685 --> 25:26.620
What's going on?

25:26.953 --> 25:29.923
You left the island. Why are you back?

25:31.157 --> 25:34.027
Does it bother you that I'm back?

25:34.361 --> 25:35.495
Of course!

25:36.696 --> 25:38.965
We just found out about your identity.

25:40.800 --> 25:41.735
Dad.

25:42.802 --> 25:44.171
What are you talking about?

25:45.672 --> 25:46.840
"Identity?"

25:50.277 --> 25:53.146
He's a murderer. He killed someone.

25:54.814 --> 25:55.849
Cha Jae Yun.

25:57.584 --> 25:58.451
Seo Anna.

25:58.952 --> 26:00.554
You... Gosh.

26:00.954 --> 26:02.088
No way.

26:02.088 --> 26:04.491
Were you seeing him
even when you knew that?

26:05.158 --> 26:07.661
Anna, what is he talking about?

26:08.929 --> 26:10.130
Deok Hyun...

26:10.497 --> 26:12.132
killed someone?

26:13.300 --> 26:14.467
One's dead,

26:14.901 --> 26:16.636
and one's in a coma.

26:17.037 --> 26:18.905
So he practically killed two people.

26:22.642 --> 26:24.211
Hey, Chief.

26:24.744 --> 26:27.948
You can't let a criminal like that
live in such a peaceful village, can you?

26:27.948 --> 26:29.683
Cha Jae Yun!

26:47.601 --> 26:48.668
I'm sorry.

26:50.470 --> 26:51.938
I couldn't bring myself to tell you.

26:53.773 --> 26:54.774
I'll...

26:55.575 --> 26:56.877
leave this island today.

26:58.011 --> 26:58.845
Good!

27:00.046 --> 27:01.548
You should've done this
a long time ago.

27:07.621 --> 27:08.855
You should've told us...

27:10.524 --> 27:13.059
when you came to this village
three years ago.

27:25.539 --> 27:26.907
It must have been tough...

27:28.408 --> 27:29.576
enduring it all alone.

27:36.249 --> 27:37.317
Right.

27:38.051 --> 27:40.487
We've seen you for years.

27:40.487 --> 27:43.423
All he's done is dive
for three whole years.

27:44.925 --> 27:47.127
We know how to use the internet too.

27:47.694 --> 27:50.297
We already looked into everything
that happened.

27:50.764 --> 27:51.598
You've gone through a lot.

27:52.165 --> 27:53.233
It must've been tough.

27:56.570 --> 27:58.905
What are you all saying?

27:59.840 --> 28:02.075
This bastard killed people!

28:04.778 --> 28:05.712
Damn it!

28:07.047 --> 28:08.481
Hey, Seo Anna. Come here.

28:09.816 --> 28:10.650
Anna!

28:14.721 --> 28:15.622
Let go of me.

28:16.056 --> 28:16.923
Let go.

28:18.091 --> 28:19.860
I used to be a professional swimmer.

28:19.860 --> 28:20.894
Is that so?

28:22.362 --> 28:23.730
- I did judo.
- What?

28:36.243 --> 28:37.377
Until elementary school.

28:37.377 --> 28:39.779
- Great job!
- Wow, you're so strong.

28:40.113 --> 28:41.248
That jerk.

28:41.548 --> 28:44.818
Anyway, since you're back,

28:45.051 --> 28:47.621
don't even think about running away,
and live a proper life.

28:47.988 --> 28:48.889
All right?

28:49.856 --> 28:50.790
He's right.

28:51.191 --> 28:55.028
Young men are rare
in this village, you know.

28:55.862 --> 28:57.030
Got that?

28:57.030 --> 28:58.031
Right!

28:58.431 --> 29:00.233
- Life isn't anything special.
- Hear, hear.

29:00.700 --> 29:02.569
It's just learning
how to get along with others.

29:02.569 --> 29:04.237
That's all.

29:04.237 --> 29:05.138
He's right.

29:06.873 --> 29:07.841
Where are the rice cakes?

29:09.276 --> 29:10.210
Where are they?

29:11.211 --> 29:12.679
They should have rice cakes.

29:12.679 --> 29:14.548
When you move in,

29:15.015 --> 29:17.551
it's customary to hand out rice cakes
to your neighbors.

29:17.551 --> 29:18.485
Right.

29:18.718 --> 29:19.619
Here.

29:19.619 --> 29:21.321
I gave him some yesterday.

29:21.321 --> 29:22.989
That was Anna's.

29:24.624 --> 29:25.725
You should eat some too.

29:27.961 --> 29:28.829
Here.

29:30.096 --> 29:30.964
Eat up!

29:33.700 --> 29:35.101
Good. Eat up.

29:37.404 --> 29:38.405
Do you want some?

29:38.405 --> 29:40.907
It's fine. Give it to the kids.

29:43.310 --> 29:44.711
Like the elders said,

29:45.412 --> 29:46.479
perhaps life really isn't...

29:47.347 --> 29:48.548
anything special.

29:49.449 --> 29:51.051
It's customary to go around...

29:51.051 --> 29:53.253
greeting your neighbors
when you move into a village.

29:55.088 --> 29:57.991
Don't cry.

29:58.358 --> 30:00.861
You're a grown man. Don't cry.

30:00.861 --> 30:01.928
It's all right.

30:02.596 --> 30:04.631
It's okay.

30:05.565 --> 30:06.399
There's no need to cry.

30:06.399 --> 30:08.535
We're glad you're back.

30:10.237 --> 30:11.438
Oh, dear.

30:11.438 --> 30:12.639
Pent-up feelings...

30:13.306 --> 30:14.541
and tangled emotions...

30:15.542 --> 30:16.943
all softened up...

30:17.511 --> 30:19.045
just with a bite of rice cake.

30:33.827 --> 30:35.462
Hey, that's pretty far.

30:36.563 --> 30:37.397
I'm not doing this.

30:38.665 --> 30:41.134
I'm pissed that I'm the only one
who didn't hear...

30:41.601 --> 30:42.536
about Deok Hyun.

30:43.069 --> 30:43.937
Whatever.

30:43.937 --> 30:45.438
Our real training starts today.

30:46.106 --> 30:47.374
This is the starting point,

30:47.374 --> 30:48.508
and that net is the turnaround point.

30:49.409 --> 30:51.211
The loser buys dinner.

30:51.678 --> 30:52.812
- What do you say?
- What?

30:53.246 --> 30:54.214
Let's go!

30:54.748 --> 30:55.749
Hey!

30:55.749 --> 30:58.585
Paying for four people
is going to cost a fortune!

31:01.288 --> 31:02.455
Hey, it's raining.

31:03.023 --> 31:03.924
Darn it.

31:04.257 --> 31:05.258
Seo Anna!

31:05.692 --> 31:06.760
Let's go home.

31:27.547 --> 31:28.915
- What do we do?
- Let's head back.

31:29.916 --> 31:31.351
Wait for me!

31:35.388 --> 31:36.256
Hurry up.

31:42.496 --> 31:43.697
Give it to me.

31:46.500 --> 31:47.901
Say "please."

31:49.302 --> 31:50.237
You little...

31:51.771 --> 31:52.839
All right.

31:54.608 --> 31:55.642
You're so slow!

31:57.344 --> 31:59.279
I can't do this.

32:02.782 --> 32:05.652
- Hold on tight!
- I can't!

32:05.652 --> 32:06.987
I'm not doing this!

32:19.599 --> 32:20.600
Hello.

32:20.600 --> 32:22.269
I'm a participant
in the swimming competition.

32:22.602 --> 32:24.571
Is the competition canceled?

32:25.105 --> 32:27.040
We'll have to wait until tomorrow to know.

32:28.375 --> 32:30.110
But the competition's tomorrow.

32:30.110 --> 32:31.978
Some forecasts say
the typhoon's moving quickly,

32:31.978 --> 32:35.115
so it'll soon be out
of our range of impact.

32:36.683 --> 32:37.517
I see.

32:39.085 --> 32:40.487
No matter how hard we try,

32:40.487 --> 32:42.789
we can't predict what lies
just a step ahead.

32:49.930 --> 32:50.797
All we can do...

32:51.665 --> 32:53.567
is to live with whatever comes our way.

33:03.643 --> 33:05.745
(Tongyeong Open Water
Swimming Competition)

33:05.745 --> 33:07.781
(Congratulations
on completing the course!)

33:17.190 --> 33:18.658
Well, this arch is here,

33:19.159 --> 33:21.795
so maybe the competition
will go as planned.

33:22.295 --> 33:23.897
The weather's cleared up.

33:24.531 --> 33:25.966
- I'm sure they'll do it.
- No,

33:26.266 --> 33:27.234
I think it's canceled.

33:27.634 --> 33:29.069
May I have your attention, please?

33:29.503 --> 33:32.072
The open water swimming competition
scheduled for today...

33:32.072 --> 33:34.007
has been cancelled...

33:34.007 --> 33:35.742
due to safety concerns...

33:35.742 --> 33:37.844
caused by strong offshore currents.

33:38.078 --> 33:40.847
All entry fees will be fully refunded,

33:40.847 --> 33:43.216
and we sincerely thank you all...

33:43.216 --> 33:44.885
for taking the time to attend.

33:45.652 --> 33:46.953
Yes, I got it right!

33:47.487 --> 33:48.688
That's nothing to be happy about!

33:49.222 --> 33:50.857
We trained so hard.

33:51.958 --> 33:54.160
What do we do, Deok Hyun?

33:54.928 --> 33:55.962
We have no choice.

33:56.463 --> 33:57.931
- Let's head back.
- No.

33:59.065 --> 34:01.535
We came all the way here.
We can't go back already.

34:02.802 --> 34:04.271
Let's do the competition...

34:05.539 --> 34:07.040
- by ourselves.
- What?

34:07.774 --> 34:08.708
By ourselves?

34:09.342 --> 34:10.544
There are participants,

34:10.544 --> 34:11.845
we're all in our swimsuits,

34:11.845 --> 34:12.812
and the ocean's right there.

34:12.812 --> 34:14.014
There's no reason why we can't.

34:14.014 --> 34:15.348
But they said it's dangerous.

34:15.649 --> 34:17.350
We can stay within the safe area.

34:18.251 --> 34:19.286
How about until that buoy?

34:20.053 --> 34:22.289
The buoy?

34:25.058 --> 34:26.393
All right, then!

34:27.127 --> 34:30.263
Let's begin our first Parang-ri...

34:30.697 --> 34:31.765
swimming competition.

34:32.132 --> 34:34.868
The loser has to do the dishes
for a month!

34:34.868 --> 34:36.870
Ready, go!

34:37.170 --> 34:38.238
Jeez.

34:38.238 --> 34:40.774
She's being childish again.

34:44.344 --> 34:45.412
Still, I won't lose to you...

34:45.412 --> 34:47.247
- Hey!
- Hey!

34:47.247 --> 34:50.250
Hey, that's cheating!

35:30.390 --> 35:32.592
Life is unpredictable,

35:33.293 --> 35:34.861
like the ocean's weather.

35:38.365 --> 35:41.001
So maybe we just have to live
as life leads us,

35:41.601 --> 35:43.336
letting the waves carry us.

35:47.307 --> 35:48.175
But...

35:48.775 --> 35:50.377
living like that is okay.

35:56.650 --> 35:58.185
We just need to live...

35:59.686 --> 36:02.222
while doing what we can,
as much as we can.

36:27.547 --> 36:29.082
Because youth isn't temporary.

36:29.783 --> 36:30.817
It lasts a lifetime.

36:33.186 --> 36:35.622
And today is always spring,

36:36.122 --> 36:37.157
always green.

36:44.231 --> 36:45.398
So we hope it's always...

36:46.299 --> 36:48.001
an azure spring.

36:55.675 --> 37:01.381
(Azure Spring)

37:09.322 --> 37:10.357
Come on! Hurry!

37:12.626 --> 37:13.393
Come on!

37:13.760 --> 37:15.295
Hurry up.

37:15.295 --> 37:16.563
- Get ready!
- Where do I look?

37:16.563 --> 37:17.597
One, two!

37:55.335 --> 38:01.241
(Thank you for supporting
and watching Azure Spring.)

38:27.501 --> 38:29.503
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
